{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789374476,"nonce":"pkTddZp8pepSs4ZfJsELdsLAKgU=","title":"A typed closure over a host entry called by record","message":"A host can bind a native by record (ba5277f): one C entry for every\nsignature, the tiers writing the arguments as one word each. A closure\nvalue had no such form. A host function reaching Haxe was a var-args\nclosure (`hlp_make_var_args`), so calling it through a typed function\nvariable meant `hlp_dyn_call` boxing every argument and packing an array,\nand casting it to a typed function type failed outright, since Ash has no\nwrapper-code generator behind `hlp_make_fun_wrapper`. On caribou's interop\nbench a Wren function called from Haxe cost 54 ns against 3.7 for a Haxe\nclosure, two allocations of it before the bridge.\n\nFix: `RecordClosure` (std/fun.rs, re-exported from `native_lib` beside\n`HostNative`) is what a closure over a record entry is bound to: the entry\nand context, and the signature's shape as `ash_native_call::pattern_of`\nfolds it. `hlp_alloc_record_closure(t, rc)` makes the closure of the full\ntype `t`, bound value first, with `fun_record` as its `fun`. `fun_record`\nis one naked entry for every signature (aarch64, x86_64 SysV): it keeps\nthe argument registers, and `record_call` places them by the pattern and\ncalls the entry; the result word goes back in x0 and d0 (rax and xmm0),\nand the caller reads the one its signature names. Compiled code calls it\nas any closure; `hlp_call_method` routes a dynamic call through\n`hlp_dyn_call`, which builds the full-type call; the interpreter's\n`CallClosure` recognises `_fun_record` as it does `_fun_var_args` and\ncalls the entry by record under a trap. A signature that does not fit\nthe registers (over eight arguments, or more integers or floats than\nthey hold) gets null, and the host falls back to var-args. Other targets\nget an entry that raises.\n\nTest: `fun::record_tests`, a `(bound, Float, Int) -\u003e Float` closure called\nas its type and through `hlp_dyn_call`.","files":null}]}